{
  // Type-checks the test and story files under `src/`, and emits nothing.
  //
  // `tsconfig.app.json` excludes `**/*.test.ts`, `**/*.test.tsx` and
  // `**/*.stories.tsx`, so before this file existed NO web test or story file
  // was type-checked by anything. `pnpm test` runs through vitest/esbuild,
  // which strips types without checking them. That is issue #340: a required
  // argument added to a source file is enforced at every source call site and
  // at none of the test call sites.
  //
  // Why a separate config and NOT a wider `include` in `tsconfig.app.json`:
  // that config is the one `tsc -b` builds. Adding these files to it would put
  // test code in the build graph. `apps/server/tsconfig.scripts.json` carries
  // the same note for the same reason. **Do not merge the two.**
  //
  // THE TWO PASSES OVERLAP HERE, unlike `apps/server`'s. Test files import
  // from `src`, so TypeScript pulls those source files into this program and
  // checks them a second time. Measured 2026-10-30: 1390 files in the
  // `tsconfig.app.json` pass, 1728 in this one. The cost is recorded in the
  // root CLAUDE.md.
  //
  // THREE THINGS IN `include` THAT ARE NOT OBVIOUS, each measured:
  //
  // 1. `src/main.tsx` holds the TanStack Router `Register` interface
  //    augmentation (main.tsx:51). Without it in the program, every
  //    `navigate({ search: (prev) => … })` callback loses its type and reports
  //    TS7006 `Parameter 'prev' implicitly has an 'any' type` — in SOURCE
  //    files, which are clean under `tsconfig.app.json`. Measured: 4 such
  //    errors in `src/routes/cooking.tsx` and 2 in
  //    `src/components/recipe/CookingControlBar/CookingControlBar.tsx`.
  //
  // 2. `src/test` holds `setup.ts`, whose first line is
  //    `import '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest'`. That import is what
  //    declares `toBeInTheDocument`, `toHaveTextContent` and the rest on
  //    vitest's `Assertion`. No test file imports it — vitest loads it through
  //    `setupFiles` — so without `src/test` in the program the matchers are
  //    unknown. Measured: 1704 extra errors across 235 files.
  //
  // 3. `vitest/globals` in `types`, because `vitest.config.ts` sets
  //    `globals: true`, so `describe` / `it` / `expect` / `vi` are ambient.
  //
  // THE `exclude` LIST BELOW IS A BACKLOG, NOT A POLICY. These 95 files
  // carry 172 pre-existing type errors across 72 of them (measured 2026-10-30,
  // plus the knock-on files described next). Fixing them is issue #340 step 3,
  // file by file. 263 of the 358 test and story files ARE checked. Removing a
  // file from this list is the unit of that work.
  //
  // It was 115 files and 726 errors when this config was added.
  //
  // Wave 1 of step 3 removed the six biggest — lib/quantityUtils.test.ts (148
  // errors), components/item/ItemCard/ItemCard.test.tsx (95),
  // lib/importData.test.ts (64), lib/sortUtils.test.ts (46),
  // db/operations.test.ts (30) and lib/filterUtils.test.ts (22) — 405 of the
  // 726, leaving 109 files and 321 errors.
  //
  // Wave 2 removed the next 14, which held 149 of those 321 (46%):
  // routes/index.test.tsx (21), lib/tagSortUtils.test.ts (17),
  // lib/expiration.test.ts (16), routes/cooking.test.tsx (14),
  // hooks/useItems.cloud.test.tsx (13), routes/items/$id/stock.test.tsx (9),
  // components/item/ItemForm/ItemForm.test.tsx (9), lib/tagUtils.test.ts (8),
  // hooks/useLocations.test.tsx (8),
  // components/item/QuickUpdateDialog/QuickUpdateDialog.test.tsx (8),
  // hooks/useShoppingCart.test.ts (7),
  // components/item/ItemFilters/ItemFilters.test.tsx (7),
  // routes/items/$id/relation/tags.test.tsx (6) and
  // hooks/usePostLoginMigration.test.ts (6).
  //
  // `hooks/useShoppingCart.test.ts` is the file issue #340 was FILED for: three
  // of its `useCheckout` calls omitted the required `items` argument and the
  // whole gate stayed green. It is now checked.
  //
  // TO MEASURE THE BACKLOG YOURSELF: copy this file and replace the `exclude`
  // array with `[]`, then run `tsc -p` on the copy. Do NOT strip the comments
  // with a regex on `//` — it eats the `/**/` inside `src/**/*.test.ts` and
  // turns the include into `src*.test.ts`, which checks ZERO files and reports
  // ONE error. A suspiciously small number is a broken probe, not good news.
  //
  // TWO TRAPS WHEN EDITING THIS LIST:
  //
  // a. `exclude` only removes a file from the program's ROOT set. A file that
  //    an INCLUDED file imports is still pulled in and still checked. That is
  //    why 23 clean `*.stories.test.tsx` smoke tests are on this list: each
  //    one calls `composeStories` on a `*.stories.tsx` that is excluded, so
  //    excluding the story alone left 45 errors reported. The pair has to move
  //    together, in both directions.
  //
  // b. `src/hooks/useItems.test.ts` and `src/hooks/useItems.test.tsx` both
  //    exist. TypeScript's `include` expansion keeps only ONE file per path
  //    minus extension, and `.ts` wins, so `useItems.test.tsx` is INVISIBLE to
  //    this config while `useItems.test.ts` is in the root set. Both are
  //    excluded here. When the `.ts` one is fixed and removed, the `.tsx` one
  //    disappears from the program again — check it by hand.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // No `tsBuildInfoFile` and no `incremental`: this config is run with
    // `tsc -p`, not `tsc -b`, so it writes no build info and re-checks
    // everything on every run.
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["vite/client", "vite-plugin-pwa/client", "vitest/globals"]
  },
  "include": [
    "src/main.tsx",
    "src/test",
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.tsx",
    "src/**/*.stories.tsx"
  ],
  "exclude": [
